<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  HuttEyes_Slitted.xml                       Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-11
  ============================================================================

  THE OBSERVATION
  ===============
  Observed in-game 2026-08-11: Hutts spawn with huge round glowing eyes, the
  same read as the Jawa. Wrong for the species. Hutts have heavy-lidded,
  cat-like eyes with vertical slit pupils.

  WHAT BTD_Hutt CARRIES TODAY
  ===========================
      guy762_Eyes_BigRed   guy762_Eyes_BigOrange
      guy762_Eyes_BigYellow  guy762_Eyes_BigGreen

  Four of them, all children of the abstract GeneEyeColor, whose exclusionTags
  are [EyeColor]. So the engine already picks exactly ONE per pawn and the Hutt
  already rolls a random eye colour. This patch does not introduce that
  mechanism, it re-points it. Proven on our own Jawa the same day: 31 pawns came
  out 16 amber / 8 orange / 7 yellow from three listed genes.

  THE REPLACEMENT
  ===============
  [LFS] Genes Expanded  Eyes (LazyFridayStudio.GenesExpandedEyes) ships 75
  feline and 75 reptile eye genes, all vertical-slit, all
  ParentName="GeneEyeColor", so they drop straight into the same slot.

  Chosen six, warm and bright per the owner's brief (reds, oranges, brights):

      Eyes_FireRed_Feline       Eyes_MarsRed_Feline
      Eyes_BurntOrange_Feline   Eyes_Tangerine_Feline
      Eyes_TaxiCab_Feline       Eyes_MidasGold_Feline

  Green is deliberately dropped. Hutt skin in this stack is already green,
  lime, sage or dark green (BTD_Hutt carries seven skin genes), and green eyes
  on green skin was part of why the face read flat.

  WHY FELINE AND NOT REPTILE
  ==========================
  Both are vertical-slit. Feline reads as a rounder pupil with a soft slit,
  reptile as a hard narrow one. Hutts are amphibian-sluglike rather than
  lizardlike, so feline is the closer match. Swapping the suffix _Feline to
  _Reptile on all six is a one-line change if it looks wrong on screen.

  ⚠️ FACIAL ANIMATION IS THE POINT. BTD_Hutt is deliberately NOT in FA's
  IgnoreEnableAnimationForRaceXenoTypeListAA — the owner likes the animated
  eyebrows. These genes were chosen because the mod ships FA compatibility:
  Compatibility/FacialAnimation/1.5/Defs/FAFelineEyes.xml declares an
  EyeballColorDef per gene, mapping it to an FA eyeball colour, so FA draws the
  right colour instead of overriding it. That folder IS loaded on 1.6: the
  mod's v1.6 LoadFolders block points at the 1.5 compat folder deliberately,
  gated on IfModActive="Nals.FacialAnimation".

  JAWA ARE NOT TOUCHED. Their huge glowing eyes are canon, confirmed working
  and confirmed liked. This patch names BTD_Hutt only.

  SAFETY AND LOAD ORDER
  =====================
  Wrapped in PatchOperationFindMod so the whole thing is a silent no-op if the
  LFS mod is ever removed  otherwise we would be adding references to genes
  that do not exist. The removals sit inside the same guard on purpose: without
  the LFS genes available, removing the stock four would leave Hutts with no
  eye gene at all.

  Every op is additionally PatchOperationConditional on the exact node, so a
  Xenotype REMIX update that changes the gene list makes this fall silent
  rather than fail. BTD_Hutt is defined by Xenotype REMIX at load 555 and
  Jawa_Patches is 564.

  VERIFY AFTER THE NEXT LOAD
  ==========================
    * Spawn a dozen Hutts. Vertical slit pupils, warm colours, no round
      glowing eyes, no green.
    * Colours vary between individuals  that is the exclusionTags roll.
    * Eyebrows still animate. If they stopped, FA lost the pawn and the
      EyeballColorDef mapping is not being found.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>[LFS] Genes Expanded - Eyes</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- 1. Drop the four big round glowing eye genes -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>/Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="BTD_Hutt"]/genes/li[text()="guy762_Eyes_BigRed"]</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
            <xpath>/Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="BTD_Hutt"]/genes/li[text()="guy762_Eyes_BigRed"]</xpath>
          </match>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>/Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="BTD_Hutt"]/genes/li[text()="guy762_Eyes_BigOrange"]</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
            <xpath>/Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="BTD_Hutt"]/genes/li[text()="guy762_Eyes_BigOrange"]</xpath>
          </match>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>/Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="BTD_Hutt"]/genes/li[text()="guy762_Eyes_BigYellow"]</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
            <xpath>/Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="BTD_Hutt"]/genes/li[text()="guy762_Eyes_BigYellow"]</xpath>
          </match>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>/Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="BTD_Hutt"]/genes/li[text()="guy762_Eyes_BigGreen"]</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
            <xpath>/Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="BTD_Hutt"]/genes/li[text()="guy762_Eyes_BigGreen"]</xpath>
          </match>
        </li>

        <!-- 2. Add the warm slitted palette -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>/Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="BTD_Hutt"]/genes[not(li[text()="Eyes_FireRed_Feline"])]</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
            <xpath>/Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="BTD_Hutt"]/genes[not(li[text()="Eyes_FireRed_Feline"])]</xpath>
            <value>
              <li>Eyes_FireRed_Feline</li>
              <li>Eyes_MarsRed_Feline</li>
              <li>Eyes_BurntOrange_Feline</li>
              <li>Eyes_Tangerine_Feline</li>
              <li>Eyes_TaxiCab_Feline</li>
              <li>Eyes_MidasGold_Feline</li>
            </value>
          </match>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
